---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import ArticleSchema from '../../components/ArticleSchema.astro';
import FaqSection from '../../components/FaqSection.astro';
import { site } from '../../content';
const path = '/compare/postscript-vs-activecampaign';
const title = 'Postscript vs ActiveCampaign for Shopify campaigns (2026)';
const desc = 'Compare Shopify campaign fit, conditional email and SMS availability, permission, purchase exits and matched pilot economics.';
const faqs = [
  {
    "question": "Which supplier should a Shopify merchant evaluate?",
    "answer": "Evaluate Postscript for Shopify-focused SMS operations and ActiveCampaign for email automation with eligible SMS and Shopify data. Select against your actual account and campaign tests, not a universal ranking."
  },
  {
    "question": "Is Postscript still SMS-only?",
    "answer": "No. Postscript has announced Email and maintains a waitlist. Confirm account access and required functionality before replacing an existing email sender."
  },
  {
    "question": "Does ActiveCampaign support SMS?",
    "answer": "Yes, with an SMS add-on and country-dependent capabilities. Broadcast and automation eligibility differ; verify your product, plan, sender registration and destination countries."
  },
  {
    "question": "Is Shopify integration access universal?",
    "answer": "No. ActiveCampaign documentation differs on plan descriptions and historical sync eligibility. Confirm the exact integration and history available in your account before migration."
  },
  {
    "question": "Must I pair either supplier with Sequenzy?",
    "answer": "No. A separate email provider is optional. Keep it only if its tested capabilities and total costs justify the coordination work, with one owner per message job."
  },
  {
    "question": "Can an imported phone number receive promotional texts?",
    "answer": "Only when channel-specific permission evidence supports that use. An email opt-in, purchase or loyalty membership does not establish SMS permission."
  },
  {
    "question": "How should a purchase stop a queued promotion?",
    "answer": "Recheck authoritative order state before dispatch, invalidate pending work, and test retries after a purchase. Delayed events must not reopen a completed journey."
  },
  {
    "question": "What should happen during a handoff?",
    "answer": "Pause entry, retire queued work at the old sender, reconcile suppression and identity records, and activate one approved owner. Rollback must keep opt-outs and purchase exits intact."
  },
  {
    "question": "Which supplier has better economics?",
    "answer": "Use matched eligible cohorts and a holdout with the same time window. Compare incremental contribution after message, platform, implementation and operator costs; supplier-attributed sales alone do not establish lift."
  }
];
---
<BaseLayout title={title} description={desc} site={site} path={path}>
  <ArticleSchema title={title} description={desc} siteName={site.name} domain={site.domain} path={path} />
  <section class="container py-14 md:py-20">
    <nav class="mb-8 text-sm"><a class="link" href="/compare">Comparisons</a> / Postscript vs ActiveCampaign</nav>
    <header class="max-w-4xl">
      <p class="badge">Shopify campaign decision</p>
      <h1 class="hero-title mt-5">Postscript vs ActiveCampaign</h1>
      <p class="mt-7 text-xl leading-9">Evaluate Postscript for Shopify-focused SMS operations and ActiveCampaign for email automation with eligible SMS and Shopify data. The better fit depends on access, event quality and the jobs your team can operate reliably.</p>
    </header>
    <article class="prose-shopify mt-12 max-w-4xl">
      <h2>Current supplier scope and access</h2>
      <p>Checked November 25, 2026: <a class="link" href="https://postscript.io/launch">Postscript announces Email</a>, while its <a class="link" href="https://postscript.io/email">Email page retains a waitlist</a>. An announcement does not establish access for your account. Confirm email availability, migration scope and required workflows before retiring an existing sender.</p>
      <p><a class="link" href="https://help.activecampaign.com/hc/en-us/articles/23392030859164-SMS-supported-countries">ActiveCampaign documents an SMS add-on</a>. Its automation destinations and broadcast eligibility differ; the cited broadcast scope is Australia, the United Kingdom and the United States. Verify current product, plan, destination and sender approval for your intended traffic.</p>
      <p>The <a class="link" href="https://help.activecampaign.com/hc/en-us/articles/115000202150-Connect-your-Shopify-store-to-ActiveCampaign">Shopify connection guide</a> describes order and customer data for follow-up email, segmentation and automations, with historical sync unavailable on Starter. The separate <a class="link" href="https://help.activecampaign.com/hc/en-us/articles/224933707-Ways-to-integrate-with-Shopify">integration overview</a> lists Deep Data on Marketing Plus, Professional and Enterprise. These descriptions are not a universal entitlement: ask the supplier to confirm your account's integration, historical data and features.</p>
      <h2>Choose against the operating job</h2>
      <table class="data-table">
        <thead><tr><th>Decision</th><th>Postscript candidate fit</th><th>ActiveCampaign candidate fit</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td>Shopify campaigns</td><td>Shopify-focused SMS when permission, event and dispatch tests pass</td><td>Email automation and eligible SMS when Shopify fields and timing pass</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Email ownership</td><td>Evaluate announced Email only after account access is confirmed</td><td>Evaluate email journeys alongside the required SMS add-on and integration</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Coordination</td><td>One approved owner per job, shared suppression if tools are split</td><td>The same rule applies even within one platform</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
      <p>Neither a second sender nor a Sequenzy pairing is mandatory. An optional email provider must earn its place through tested requirements and total cost. Compare <a class="link" href="/apps/postscript">Postscript</a> and <a class="link" href="/apps/activecampaign">ActiveCampaign</a> against the same acceptance record.</p>
      <h2>Fourteen fictional proposed merchant fixtures</h2>
      <p>Every named merchant below is a fictional proposed test fixture, not a customer, testimonial, observed result or supplier capability guarantee. Both fits are conditional on account access, supported events and successful tests. Apply the shared release controls below to every fixture.</p>
      <h3>SoleDrop ATX: size-specific sneaker early access</h3>
      <p>Proposed test: recheck the requested size and available-to-sell stock before releasing each waitlist cohort. Postscript may fit Shopify SMS cohorts; ActiveCampaign may fit Shopify-data segmentation. Approve only after the relevant account demonstrates this job, including cancellation after purchase and duplicate-event replay.</p>
      <h3>Festival Threads Co: city-specific tour merchandise</h3>
      <p>Proposed test: use the venue date and recipient timezone; expire messages after the show. Postscript may fit targeted SMS schedules; ActiveCampaign may fit email-led city journeys with eligible SMS. Approve only after the relevant account demonstrates this job, including cancellation after purchase and duplicate-event replay.</p>
      <h3>Vinyl Vault Records: collector access to limited pressings</h3>
      <p>Proposed test: derive collector tiers from settled orders and exclude canceled or refunded purchases. Postscript may fit collector SMS cohorts; ActiveCampaign may fit order-based email and SMS branches. Approve only after the relevant account demonstrates this job, including cancellation after purchase and duplicate-event replay.</p>
      <h3>Bloom & Wick: holiday gifting deadlines</h3>
      <p>Proposed test: separate gift intent from self-purchase and validate fulfillment cutoffs. Postscript may fit deadline SMS; ActiveCampaign may fit gift education email with eligible SMS reminders. Approve only after the relevant account demonstrates this job, including cancellation after purchase and duplicate-event replay.</p>
      <h3>Peak Trail Gear: clearance without automatic VIP discounts</h3>
      <p>Proposed test: separate bargain-sensitive cohorts from full-price loyalists and reserve a holdout. Postscript may fit targeted clearance SMS; ActiveCampaign may fit conditional email and SMS offers. Approve only after the relevant account demonstrates this job, including cancellation after purchase and duplicate-event replay.</p>
      <h3>Sauce Lab: batch scarcity alerts</h3>
      <p>Proposed test: use current batch inventory, expire stale scarcity claims and stop after sellout. Postscript may fit batch SMS alerts; ActiveCampaign may fit inventory-informed automation if events are available. Approve only after the relevant account demonstrates this job, including cancellation after purchase and duplicate-event replay.</p>
      <h3>Ember Ceramics: fair access to a small kiln release</h3>
      <p>Proposed test: retain waitlist ordering outside send timing; messages must not promise reserved stock. Postscript may fit SMS access notices; ActiveCampaign may fit maker-story email and access branches. Approve only after the relevant account demonstrates this job, including cancellation after purchase and duplicate-event replay.</p>
      <h3>Ridge Run Coffee: subscription and flash-offer separation</h3>
      <p>Proposed test: check the subscription system and suppress active subscribers from incompatible flash offers. Postscript may fit subscriber-aware SMS if fields are available; ActiveCampaign may fit subscription-aware email and SMS if fields are available. Approve only after the relevant account demonstrates this job, including cancellation after purchase and duplicate-event replay.</p>
      <h3>Cipher Audio: education before a high-value launch</h3>
      <p>Proposed test: join lawful browse intent to a known identity without treating browsing as SMS consent. Postscript may fit permissioned launch SMS; ActiveCampaign may fit education email with eligible SMS launch notices. Approve only after the relevant account demonstrates this job, including cancellation after purchase and duplicate-event replay.</p>
      <h3>Patchwork Denim: one-of-one style alerts</h3>
      <p>Proposed test: match explicit style preferences, recheck the unique item and cancel all pending alerts after sale. Postscript may fit preference-based SMS; ActiveCampaign may fit preference-based email and eligible SMS. Approve only after the relevant account demonstrates this job, including cancellation after purchase and duplicate-event replay.</p>
      <h3>Arena Energy: athlete collaboration with channel-specific offers</h3>
      <p>Proposed test: approve the offer version and prevent an email-only gift from appearing in SMS. Postscript may fit approved timing texts; ActiveCampaign may fit offer education email and eligible timing texts. Approve only after the relevant account demonstrates this job, including cancellation after purchase and duplicate-event replay.</p>
      <h3>Loom & Frame: edition sell-through notices</h3>
      <p>Proposed test: calculate availability from the edition ledger and exclude buyers before any reminder. Postscript may fit collector SMS notices; ActiveCampaign may fit collector email and SMS branches. Approve only after the relevant account demonstrates this job, including cancellation after purchase and duplicate-event replay.</p>
      <h3>Driftwood Surf Co: seasonal content and restock waitlists</h3>
      <p>Proposed test: keep forecast content separate from actual restock confirmation and expire outdated alerts. Postscript may fit restock SMS; ActiveCampaign may fit seasonal email with eligible restock SMS. Approve only after the relevant account demonstrates this job, including cancellation after purchase and duplicate-event replay.</p>
      <h3>Noir Collective: scheduled VIP streetwear releases</h3>
      <p>Proposed test: coordinate early-access and general windows with a shared frequency budget. Postscript may fit VIP SMS cohorts; ActiveCampaign may fit email and SMS release journeys. Approve only after the relevant account demonstrates this job, including cancellation after purchase and duplicate-event replay.</p>
      <h2>Shared permission, identity and release controls</h2>
      <p>For every fixture, retain channel-specific permission source, timestamp, disclosure and withdrawal history. Quarantine records with missing evidence. Keep email and SMS permission distinct; resolve Shopify customer IDs, email addresses and normalized phone numbers without merging unrelated people or restoring withdrawn permission. Unknown identity or timezone means hold for review.</p>
      <p>Use Shopify order IDs and explicit paid, canceled, refunded and returned states as order truth; subscription and edition systems remain authoritative for their own facts. Recheck permission, stock, offer expiry and purchase exits immediately before dispatch. Test delayed and out-of-order events, repeat webhooks, guest checkout, merged profiles, purchases between scheduling and sending, and unsubscribe during a retry.</p>
      <p>Give each job a single sending owner and a stable customer/job/event key. Deduplicate retries across workers and suppliers, record dispatch status, bound retries and route exhausted work to a named operator. Do not blindly resend after an ambiguous timeout. Retire queued reminders and scheduled broadcasts at the old owner; disabling new entries alone does not cancel pending work.</p>
      <p>The campaign owner approves copy, offer, audience and expiry; the data owner signs off identity and order reconciliation; the sending owner verifies destination eligibility, quiet-hour policy, registration, replies and opt-out propagation. Test applicable recipient rules with qualified advice instead of treating a generic quiet-hour window as universal compliance. See <a class="link" href="/guides/consent">permission records</a> and <a class="link" href="/guides/email-sms-coordination">channel coordination</a>.</p>
      <h2>Handoff and rollback acceptance</h2>
      <p>Pause entries, inventory active and queued work, export only records lawfully available, reconcile suppression and order states, and obtain evidence that old queues are canceled before enabling the new owner. Confirm any sender transfer with both suppliers; neither portability nor account export access is promised here. Run a small approved cohort and reconcile dispatch logs before increasing volume.</p>
      <p>Rollback pauses the new owner, cancels its pending work and preserves all new opt-outs, purchases and dispatch keys before restoring a validated prior configuration. Never replay a stale backlog. If access, queue cancellation or suppression reconciliation cannot be proved, keep the affected job paused and assign an operator to resolve it.</p>
      <h2>Matched hypothetical economics</h2>
      <p>This is an invented worksheet, not a quote or forecast. For either candidate, assign 1,000 eligible customers to treatment and 1,000 comparable customers to holdout for the same window and offer policy. Suppose net sales after discounts and returns are $6,000 versus $5,000, and variable product and fulfillment costs are $2,400 versus $2,000. Incremental contribution before campaign costs is ($6,000 - $2,400) - ($5,000 - $2,000) = $600.</p>
      <p>With hypothetical allocated platform/add-on costs of $100, message and carrier costs of $80, and setup plus operator/support costs of $120, contribution after campaign costs is $600 - $100 - $80 - $120 = $300, or $0.30 per treatment-eligible customer. Discounts and returns are already included in net sales; do not subtract them twice. Apply the same accounting and denominator to both suppliers, count all channels and any optional second provider, and report uncertainty rather than claiming a winner from identical assumptions.</p>
      <p>Obtain current written quotes for your contact count, countries, encoding and message segments, peak volume, email access, add-ons, integration work and migration. Repeat the model at peak load and separate one-time costs from recurring costs. See <a class="link" href="/guides/pricing">pricing economics</a>.</p>
      <h2>Decision gate</h2>
      <p>Postscript is a useful candidate when Shopify SMS operations drive the requirement and its available products pass the fixtures. ActiveCampaign is a useful candidate when email automation and eligible SMS can use the required Shopify data reliably. Choose only after permission, identity, order exits, queue retirement, deduplication, approvals, rollback and matched economics pass in the actual account. Public documentation cannot substitute for that pilot.</p>
    </article>
    <FaqSection faqs={faqs} title="Postscript vs ActiveCampaign FAQ" />
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
